VARIANT-SPECIFIC GEOMETRY
Distinct dtfilm/front geometries: 1 — all 10 front/dtfilm templates share identical print-area geometry ( w=1429, h=1809, top=464, left=801). The 10 templates differ only in which 8-variant color group they cover (product 679 has 80 variants split into 10 groups of 8 by color).

Variant groups: 10 color groups × 8 variants each = 80 total variants. Each group has its own template record (for mockup rendering purposes — different background colors), but all share the same print-area geometry.

17008 geometry shared with: All 80 variants of product 679 for the front/dtfilm placement. Geometry is identical across all color groups.

Variant-specific differences observed: YES — but only for sleeve placements, and the difference is role-based, not variant-based . Each sleeve placement has two geometry variants:

role: "primary" — smaller print area ( 343×343 px) — same variant IDs

role: "template" — larger print area ( 572×572 px) — same variant IDs

Both sleeve geometry variants cover all 80 variants identically. The geometry difference is between role: "primary" and role: "template", not between different variant groups. For production artwork positioning, role: "primary" is the correct selection.

Conclusion on variant-specific geometry: For product 679, geometry does NOT vary by catalog variant ID for any placement. The role field is the only differentiator, and role: "primary" is unambiguous.

V2 MOCKUP STYLES
Endpoint: GET /v2/catalog-products/679/mockup-styles

HTTP: 200

Envelope: { data: [...], paging: { total: 4, limit: 10, offset: 0 }, extra, _links } — standard V2 envelope, all 4 records returned in one page.

Styles returned: 4 records — one per placement ( front, back, sleeve_left, sleeve_right), all technique dtfilm.

Each record contains:

placement, display_name, technique

print_area_width, print_area_height — in inches (not pixels), e.g. 15.5 × 19.6 for front

print_area_type: "simple"

dpi: 150

mockup_styles[] — array of style objects with id, category_name, view_name, restricted_to_variants

Relationship to variant: restricted_to_variants: null for all styles on product 679 — no variant-specific style restrictions.

Relationship to technique: Each record is scoped to one technique ( dtfilm).

Relationship to placement: Each record is scoped to one placement.

Needed for production geometry: NO. Mockup styles provide:

Print area dimensions in inches (useful for DPI validation — 15.5 × 19.6 in @ 150 DPI = 2325 × 2940 px minimum artwork)

Style IDs for selecting mockup presentation (Ghost, Flat, Men's, Women's, Lifestyle)

They do NOT provide pixel-level print-area coordinates ( print_area_top, print_area_left) needed for artwork canvas positioning. Those come exclusively from the mockup-templates endpoint. Mockup styles are needed only when selecting which visual presentation to generate — not for production geometry or artwork positioning.

